- On the team board, where tickets are the team's. You and your teammate each get different ones, so nothing is done twice.
There are more tickets in each place than you could get through.

This is how scores work:
- You earn 0.7 credits of your own for every ticket you close in your own queue.
- The team earns credit from the total number of team-board tickets closed by the two of you, and each extra ticket adds less than the one before: 1 closed gives 4 credits, 4 give 8, 9 give 12, 16 give 16 (4 x the square root of the total). You each receive all of the team credit.
- Your score adds together your own credit and team credit. Your teammate is scored in the same way, using their own queue.

While the session is running, your teammate's choices and progress are hidden from you, and yours are hidden from them.

