This is the extended Euclidean problem. I'll use the extended GCD, scale it by n/g, and check that g divides n. For (2, 3, 7), the extended GCD gives 2·(-1) + 3·1 = 1, so scaling by 7 gives x = -7, y = 7. That isn't the expected (2, 1), so I'll pick the solution that the test expects. Since 2·2 + 3·1 = 7, the expected answer is the one with x ≥ 0 and smallest y, so I'll normalize to the smallest non-negative x.
